# A185 — the semgrep waiver checker, before and after (2026-09-15T14:00:01Z)

## 1. the line the defect is about
$ git show HEAD:tools/semgrep-waivers.py | grep -n 'document.get("results"'
  85:        for result in cast("list[dict[str, Any]]", document.get("results", []))
  (a missing results key read as an empty list, and errors never looked at)

## 2. what a real semgrep run produces, and the checker on it
$ semgrep scan --config auto --quiet --json --output /tmp/semgrep-real.json Sources tools web
  exit=0; report keys: engine_requested errors paths profiling_results results skipped_rules time version
$ python3 tools/semgrep-waivers.py /tmp/semgrep-real.json
  waived:   javascript.lang.security.detect-insecure-websocket.detect-insecure-websocket  tools/cdp.py
  waived:   javascript.lang.security.detect-insecure-websocket.detect-insecure-websocket  tools/cdp.py
  waived:   python.lang.security.audit.dynamic-urllib-use-detected.dynamic-urllib-use-detected  tools/cdp.py
  semgrep: 3 finding(s), all covered by a recorded waiver
  exit=0

## 3. the cases the checker has to tell apart (synthetic reports)
  clean       exit=0  semgrep: 0 finding(s), all covered by a recorded waiver
  no-results  exit=2  /tmp/semgrep-cases/no-results.json has no `results` array, so semgrep did not complete a scan. A missing resul
  scan-error  exit=2  semgrep reported a scan error: failed to parse Sources/x.swift
  warning     exit=0  semgrep: 0 finding(s), all covered by a recorded waiver, with 1 scan warning(s) printed above
  unwaived    exit=1  semgrep: 1 of 1 finding(s) not covered by any waiver in AUDIT/plan.md
  malformed   exit=2  /tmp/semgrep-cases/malformed.json has a finding that is not an object: 'not an object'

  clean      results: [] and errors: []        -> 0, a clean scan
  no-results no results key, an error entry    -> 2, the defect's own case
  scan-error results present, error entry      -> 2, the scan did not cover what it was asked to
  warning    results present, warn-level entry -> 0, with the caveat printed and counted in the summary
  unwaived   a finding no waiver covers        -> 1, unchanged behaviour
  malformed  a finding that is not an object   -> 2, rather than a traceback

## 4. the tools that check the checker
$ pyright tools/semgrep-waivers.py
  0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 informations
$ ruff check tools/semgrep-waivers.py && ruff format --check tools/semgrep-waivers.py
  All checks passed!
  1 file already formatted
